                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            physics, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            encodes the
            = succeed "-content" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle"} particle
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model (in theoretical physics)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            to the gauge bundle is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter+field"} matter field
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
          %p
            Therefore all the ingredients so far encode the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinematics"} kinematics
            of gauge theory, its setup before an actual
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            is specified.
          %p
            Dynamics in physics says how things
            = succeed "," do
              %em move
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            in a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            or more generally in some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
          %p
            Our
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metalanguage"} language
            for reasoning about physics should be able to express this. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a homotopy type that models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            (the collection of all points of spacetime) there should be a homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            and higher homotopies are the
            = succeed "," do
              %em smooth trajectories
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} smooth paths
            and higher paths in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            In order to analyse the notion of
            %em smoothness
            here – we will say: the way that points hold together by
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            – there should also be
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an expression
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat X
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete
                collection of points underlying
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
