          %h4#quantum_3d_chernsimons_theory_for_compact_simple_gauge_group Quantum 3d Chern-Simons theory for compact simple gauge group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"}> Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Turaev-Viro+construction"} Turaev-Viro construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
          %h4#higher_geometric_quantization Higher geometric quantization
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometric+quantization"} higher geometric quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
          %h3#semantics_layer Semantics Layer
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+smooth+infinity-groupoid"} n-plectic smooth infinity-groupoid
          %h3#syntactic_layer Syntactic Layer
          %p (…)
          %h2#ApplicationsToOpenQuestionsInPhysics
            %strong Application to open questions in physics
          %p
            What is it that
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
            = succeed "/local" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            and generally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory in physics
            contribute to open research questions in theoretical physics?
          %p Often when this question is asked the most glaring open question of contemporary theoretical physics is forgotten:
          %p
            %em
              What IS
              = succeed "?" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+quantum+field+theory"} local quantum field theory
          %p
            While something going by this name is clearly in use, it is just as clear that the full answer to this question is only being discovered these days, with formalizations such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theorem"} cobordism theorem
            and constructions such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebras"} factorization algebras
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-quantization"} BV-quantization
            – both of which are crucially constructions in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p Despite the huge success of quantum field theory, it it worthwhile to remember that all the fundamental open questions in present day fundamental physics quite likely require a deeper understanding of what quantum field theory actually is, notably non-perturbatively:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Why is there
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
                in non-perturbative
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            %li
              %p What is beyond-the-standard-model physics?
            %li
              %p
                What is
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            %li
              %p
                What is non-perturbative
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
            says that the bulk of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            is entirely unknown to us (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+matter"}> dark matter
            , “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+energy"}> dark energy
            ”), while at the same time the theoretical prediction what the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+energy"} vacuum energy
            should be is entirely off. How glaring an open question about the nature of quantum field theory this actually is is often forgotten due to the success of
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
          %p
            And while there is work going in this direction, it may be worthwhile to recall how relatively primitive the available theoretical tools often still are. For instance it seems clear that “canonical non-covariant quantization” can hardly be an approrpiate tool to approach anything in the direction of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            necessary to make progress here is not widely known in the theoretical physics community. Attempts to refine quantization to a “covariant” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+quantum+field+theory"}> local
            ” formalism via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
            have mainly got stuck, since local observables just do not form a sensible structure in ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+theory"} infinity-Lie theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#hgp13"} hgp 13
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LocalObservables13"} lo 13
          %p
            If one assumes that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            is part of the answer as to what underlies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} and cosmology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            of string theory are clearly objects in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            etc. For instance the natural identification of the latter as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            in (
            %a{:href => "#FSS7dCS"}> FSS7dCS
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSSCField"} FSSCField
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
            and hence the relation of string theory to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            can really be understood if such basic higher-geometric phenomena of string theory are ignored (see
            %a{:href => "#http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory#ContributionDistlerFreedMoore"} Distler-Freed-Moore 09
            on this point).
          %p (…)
          %h2#related_expositions
            %strong Related expositions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
            %li
              %p
