              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesHigherGeometricPrequantumGeometry"} Higher geometric prequantum theory
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesFurtherDetails"} Further details
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %p
            A textbook with basic introductions to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is
          %ul
            %li#Frankel
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Frankel"}> Theodore Frankel
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Geometry+of+Physics+-+An+Introduction"} The Geometry of Physics - An Introduction
          %p A discussion of aspects of quantum field theory with emphasis on the kind of modern tools that we are using here is in
          %ul
            %li#Paugam
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric+Paugam"}> Frédéric Paugam
              ,
              %em Towards the mathematics of quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://people.math.jussieu.fr/~fpaugam/documents/enseignement/master-mathematical-physics.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p The present discussion corresponds to section “1.2 Geometry of phyics” in
          %ul
            %li#SchreiberCohesiveInfinityTopos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p which gives a more comprehensive account.
          %p
            Another set of lecture notes along the above lines with an emphasis on aspects in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
            motivated from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#TwistedCohomologyLecture
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory"} twisted smooth cohomology in string theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Fields and twisted K-theory
          %p
            An exposition and survey of matters related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometric+quantization"} higher geometric quantization
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiberCSIntroAndSurvey
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
          %p The syntactic perspective above is laid out further in
          %ul
            %li#SyntheticQuantumFieldTheory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Synthetic+Quantum+Field+Theory"} Synthetic Quantum Field Theory
          %p
            see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "motivic%20quantization#GeneralAbstractTypeTheoreticSummary"} General abstract type theoretic summary
          %h3#_mathematical_quantum_field_theory Mathematical quantum field theory
          %p
            A textbook (really a collection of lecture notes) on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            that tries to present material in a conceptually clean way is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"} Pavel Etingof
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"}> David Kazhdan
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                , A course for mathematicians
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
          %p
            A collection trying to summarize the state of the art of the formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT"} QFT
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            as of 2011 is
          %ul#SatiSchreiber
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
          %h3#ReferencesToposTheory Topos theory in differential geometry and physics
          %p
            One of the central figures of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum+mechanics"} continuum mechanics
            in his case).
          %p An influential text is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Toposes of laws of notion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.acsu.buffalo.edu/~wlawvere/ToposMotion.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            which motivates
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equations"} differential equations
            appearing as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            in physics. The early text
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+Thoughts+on+the+Future+of+Category+Theory"} Some Thoughts on the Future of Category Theory
              in A. Carboni, M. Pedicchio, G. Rosolini,
              %em Category Theory
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Como"} Proceedings of the International Conference held in Como
          %p
            already sketches the formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+toposes"} cohesive toposes
            and motivates their axioms with heuristics from geometry and physics.
          %p A review by Lawvere is in
          %ul#Lawvere2000
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Comments on the Development of Topos Theory
          %p
            Modern accounts of physics in this spirit includes notably also the book (
            %a{:href => "#Paugam"}> Paugam
            ) listed above.
          %h3#ReferencesHigherCategoryTheoryInPhysics Higher category theory in physics
          %p
            An early proposal that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            should refine to a structure involving
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-vector+space"} (n-k)-vector spaces
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-k)
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebraic+Structures+and+Quantization"} Higher Algebraic Structures and Quantization
          %p
            The full formalization of this for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+topological+field+theory"} extended topological field theory
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
          %p
            Related comments on the extended
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} infinity-Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
            are in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
          %p
            For more pointers see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory and physics
          %h3#ReferencesLocalPrequantumFieldTheory Local prequantum field theory
          %p
            The idea of formulating local prequantum field theory by spans in a slice over a “space of phases” in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            has been expressed in the unpublished note
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Nonabelian+cocycles+and+their+quantum+symmetries"} Nonabelian cocycles and their quantum symmetries
              (2008)
          %p
            A formulation of the idea for
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %ul#FHLT
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
              (2010)
          %p based on the considerations in section 3.2 of
          %ul#LurieTFT
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
              (2009).
          %p
            Based on the general formulation of the more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} field theory with defects
            described in section 4.3 there, in
          %ul#FiorenzaValentino
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Valentino"} Alessandro Valentino
              %em Boundary conditions in local TFTs
              (in preparation)
          %p
            the structure of such
            = succeed "/defects/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+walls"} domain walls
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            are analyzed in the prequantum theory, hence with coefficients in an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+spans"} (∞,n)-category of spans
          %p
            The study of local prequantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            with its codimension-1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            and codimension 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+line"}> Wilson line
            \-theory in this fashion, in an ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#lpqft"}> lpqft
            )
          %p Much of the content of this entry here are, or arose as, lecture notes for
          %ul#SchreiberPittLectures
            %li
