          %h3#ReferencesFurtherDetails Further details
          %h4#ReferencesPhysicalFields Physical fields
          %p
            For references on the tradtional formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+fields"} physical fields
            by sections of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundles"} field bundles
            as discussed
            %a{:href => "#IdeaOfFieldBundlesAndItsProblems"} above
            see there references
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} there
          %p
            The formulation of physical fields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            as in the
            = succeed "-section" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Definition"} Definition
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Background+fields+in+twisted+differential+nonabelian+cohomology"} Background fields in twisted differential nonabelian cohomology
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Strings%2C+Fields%2C+Topology"} Oberwolfach Workshop, June 2009 – Strings, Fields, Topology
          %p Further articles since then are listed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p
            In particular the general notion of fields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} twisted differential c-structures
            appears in
          %ul#SSS
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
